    "_comment": "NOAA's definition: two or more cetaceans, same or mixed species, stranded at the same time and place, other than a cow-calf pair. Limited to cetaceans on purpose: several seals or sea lions on one beach is a normal haul-out. distance_km and time_hours are how close two separate incidents must be to count as one event; both are starting values and have not been checked against real strandings.",
